# OnionHost golden torrc for container A (the onion-service gateway).
# Rendered to /etc/onionhost/torrc by onionhost-generate-configs.
# Settings: PoC golden set (POC-RESULTS Gate 0) with production paths.
# PoWQueueRate/Burst CALIBRATED in step-3 slice 3 (ISO-BUILD-LOG):
# DQ3's rule - ~2x the sustained rendezvous rate (Gate 5 rig baseline
# 2.23/s, corroborated by slice-3 multi-client runs: 1.6/s at 12
# isolated-circuit clients, ~6.4/s aggregate under 48-way parallelism,
# service CPU ~2% throughout). 5/10 provably engages under a
# saturating introduction flood and is invisible under moderate load;
# the old 250/500 never engaged at any load generatable from one host
# (max attempt rate ~6.4/s). See the slice-3 log for the full table
# and the single-host caveats.
DataDirectory /var/lib/onionhost/tor/data
SocksPort 0
Log notice stderr
HiddenServiceDir /var/lib/onionhost/tor/hs
HiddenServicePort 80 unix:/run/onionhost/web/http.sock
HiddenServicePoWDefensesEnabled 1
HiddenServicePoWQueueRate 5
HiddenServicePoWQueueBurst 10
HiddenServiceEnableIntroDoSDefense 1
HiddenServiceEnableIntroDoSRatePerSec 25
HiddenServiceEnableIntroDoSBurstPerSec 200
HiddenServiceNumIntroductionPoints 3
HiddenServiceMaxStreams 50
HiddenServiceMaxStreamsCloseCircuit 1
ControlSocket /run/onionhost/control/a.sock
